//
// Light Clicking According to the Array
//


title: EarlyRelight1
---
Aren't you getting tired?
===

title: EarlyRelight2
---
I suppose it is a little scary...the 'dark'...
===

title: EarlyRelight3
---
But what truly are you afraid of?
===

title: EarlyRelight4
---
Is it change?
===

title: EarlyRelight5
---
Is it the dark?
===

title: EarlyRelight6
---
Or is it something bigger?
===

title: EarlyRelight7
---
What if we just...try?
===

title: EarlyRelight8
---
Please. You have to let go.
===


//
// Unique 9 First Darkness Dialogue Points
//


title: DarknessLowRelight
---
Rarely do things stay the same.
===

title: DarknessAfterEL1
---
It's okay to stop holding on.
===

title: DarknessAfterEL2
---
See, that wasn't so bad.
===

title: DarknessAfterEL3
---
It's okay to face those fears.
===

title: DarknessAfterEL4
---
Change is just a part of life.
===

title: DarknessAfterEL5
---
Sometimes letting go pushes us forward.
===

title: DarknessAfterEL6
---
It may feel scary at first.
===

title: DarknessAfterEL7
---
To grow we must let go.
===

title: DarknessAfterEL8
---
It's okay. You're not alone.
===


// STATE 2
// The room is still lived in, but things are changing.
// Early accepts change.
// Middle is beginning to accept it.
// Late is still holding tightly.


title: Early_Darkness2
---
Things can change without disappearing.
===

title: Middle_Darkness2
---
You noticed it too, didn't you?
===

title: Late_Darkness2
---
You can't keep everything exactly as it was.
===


// STATE 3
// Neglect begins to show. Plants are dying.
// This is the emotional low point before the larger loss becomes visible.


title: Early_Darkness3
---
Some things end, even when we care for them.
===

title: Middle_Darkness3
---
Holding on can't stop something from changing.
===

title: Late_Darkness3
---
You can't keep something alive just by refusing to let it go.
===


// STATE 4
// Moving boxes. Someone has left.
// This should be the clearest moment of loss without explicitly explaining it.


title: Early_Darkness4
---
You knew this moment would come.
===

title: Middle_Darkness4
---
It's different when the space they leave behind is real.
===

title: Late_Darkness4
---
I know. You wanted more time.
===


// STATE 5 (FINAL)
// Renewal. The room belongs to a life that is continuing.
// All three paths arrive at acceptance, but with different emotional histories.


title: Early_Darkness5
---
Look around.

Something new can grow here.
===

title: Middle_Darkness5
---
It still hurts.

But look how much has changed.
===

title: Late_Darkness5
---
You let go.

And you're still here.
===

// Relighting after the first darkness. The selected path stays locked.
// Three one-time prompts per room, at 5 / 10 / 15 relights; state 5 uses the ending instead.

title: Early_Relight1_1
---
You can miss something without wanting it back.
===

title: Early_Relight1_2
---
Sometimes you reach for it before you remember.
===

title: Early_Relight1_3
---
It takes a little getting used to, doesn't it?
===

title: Early_Relight2_1
---
What do you find yourself remembering?
===

title: Early_Relight2_2
---
The little things have a way of staying with you.
===

title: Early_Relight2_3
---
You don't have to remember every detail for it to matter.
===

title: Early_Relight3_1
---
Some days you'll miss it more than others.
===

title: Early_Relight3_2
---
Even when you thought you were doing alright.
===

title: Early_Relight3_3
---
That doesn't mean you have to start over.
===

title: Early_Relight4_1
---
There may be things you never get to say.
===

title: Early_Relight4_2
---
I know. You had imagined it differently.
===

title: Early_Relight4_3
---
You can be grateful for what happened and wish there had been more.
===

title: Early_Relight5_1
---
Was that a little easier this time?
===

title: Early_Relight5_2
---
It's okay if you didn't think about it for a while.
===

title: Early_Relight5_3
---
You haven't forgotten. You're just thinking about what comes next.
===

title: Middle_Relight1_1
---
Part of you still wants to try again.
===

title: Middle_Relight1_2
---
And part of you remembers why you stopped.
===

title: Middle_Relight1_3
---
You don't have to pretend those feelings agree.
===

title: Middle_Relight2_1
---
You keep going back to the good parts.
===

title: Middle_Relight2_2
---
Do you miss what it was, or what you hoped it would become?
===

title: Middle_Relight2_3
---
I suppose it can be hard to tell.
===

title: Middle_Relight3_1
---
You thought you'd feel differently by now.
===

title: Middle_Relight3_2
---
Then something small reminds you.
===

title: Middle_Relight3_3
---
You can have a difficult day without taking it all back.
===

title: Middle_Relight4_1
---
Still thinking of something you could have done?
===

title: Middle_Relight4_2
---
You can spend a long time finishing a conversation that's already over.
===

title: Middle_Relight4_3
---
What would you say if you weren't trying to change the ending?
===

title: Middle_Relight5_1
---
Does feeling better feel a little like betrayal?
===

title: Middle_Relight5_2
---
You don't have to keep hurting to prove it mattered.
===

title: Middle_Relight5_3
---
What would you like to do for yourself now?
===

title: Late_Relight1_1
---
You weren't ready for that to be the last time.
===

title: Late_Relight1_2
---
Maybe you thought you'd get another chance.
===

title: Late_Relight1_3
---
I know. There was still so much you wanted.
===

title: Late_Relight2_1
---
What are you hoping will happen if you keep trying?
===

title: Late_Relight2_2
---
An answer? An apology?
===

title: Late_Relight2_3
---
Or just a reason that makes it hurt a little less?
===

title: Late_Relight3_1
---
You've been carrying that feeling for a long time.
===

title: Late_Relight3_2
---
Does it feel like the last thing you have left of it?
===

title: Late_Relight3_3
---
Maybe that's why putting it down feels so difficult.
===

title: Late_Relight4_1
---
You keep asking what you could have done differently.
===

title: Late_Relight4_2
---
As if finding the right answer could give it back.
===

title: Late_Relight4_3
---
You can wish it had stayed. You don't have to keep waiting.
===

title: Late_Relight5_1
---
Who would you be if you weren't holding on to this?
===

title: Late_Relight5_2
---
You don't have to know yet.
===

title: Late_Relight5_3
---
Maybe you can give yourself a chance to find out.
===


// After the player's final relight in State 5.
title: Ending
---
What mattered still matters.
You don't have to hold on so tightly now.
There is more ahead of you.
===
